---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbe/asbe14.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. The Five-Step Model" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. Over-Time vs Point-in-Time Recognition" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. Absorbing Construction Contracts — the End of Percentage-of-Completion as a Separate Standard" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. Variable Consideration and the Transaction Price" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. Allocating the Transaction Price" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. Worked Example — Allocating a Bundled Transaction Price" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Worked Example — Over-Time Recognition for a Construction Contract" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Relationship to IFRS 15" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "15. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
</div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A landmark, closely converged revenue standard</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 14 was COMPREHENSIVELY revised in JULY 2017, INTRODUCING a UNIFIED five-STEP revenue RECOGNITION model — CLOSELY mirroring IFRS 15's OWN approach internationally, and REPLACING the OLDER, fragmented Chinese REVENUE framework that PREVIOUSLY split ordinary SALES revenue from CONSTRUCTION contract revenue (the LATTER governed SEPARATELY by ASBE No. 15 — see the COMPANION historical poster). This REVISION is ONE of the MOST significant "KEPT pace with the CURRENT international standard" examples WITHIN the ENTIRE ASBE suite.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Revenue from contracts with customers</div><div class="principle">This Standard applies to REVENUE arising from CONTRACTS with CUSTOMERS for the SALE of goods or PROVISION of services in the ORDINARY course of BUSINESS — EXCLUDING leases, INSURANCE contracts, and FINANCIAL instruments, WHICH are governed by THEIR own respective STANDARDS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>The Five-Step Model</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Directly mirroring IFRS 15's structure</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.4fr 2.6fr;"><span>Step</span><span>Description</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.4fr 2.6fr;"><span>1</span><span>IDENTIFY the CONTRACT with the CUSTOMER</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.4fr 2.6fr;"><span>2</span><span>IDENTIFY the PERFORMANCE OBLIGATIONS (distinct PROMISES) within the CONTRACT</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.4fr 2.6fr;"><span>3</span><span>DETERMINE the TRANSACTION price</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.4fr 2.6fr;"><span>4</span><span>ALLOCATE the transaction PRICE to each PERFORMANCE obligation, based on RELATIVE standalone SELLING price</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.4fr 2.6fr;"><span>5</span><span>RECOGNISE revenue AS (or WHEN) each PERFORMANCE obligation is SATISFIED</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Over-Time vs Point-in-Time Recognition</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">The successor framework to percentage-of-completion</div><div class="text-supporting">A PERFORMANCE obligation is SATISFIED OVER TIME WHERE the CUSTOMER simultaneously RECEIVES and CONSUMES benefits AS the ENTERPRISE performs, the ENTERPRISE'S performance CREATES or ENHANCES an ASSET the customer CONTROLS as it's CREATED, or the ASSET has NO alternative USE and the ENTERPRISE has an ENFORCEABLE right to PAYMENT for performance COMPLETED to date — OTHERWISE, revenue is RECOGNISED at a SINGLE point in TIME, when CONTROL transfers.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Absorbing Construction Contracts — the End of Percentage-of-Completion as a Separate Standard</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">One general model, replacing a separate construction-specific standard</div><div class="text-supporting">BEFORE this REVISION, LONG-term construction CONTRACTS were governed SEPARATELY by ASBE No. 15, APPLYING a DEDICATED percentage-of-COMPLETION methodology DISTINCT from ORDINARY sales REVENUE recognition. The 2017 revision CONSOLIDATED both TOPICS into THIS single, UNIFIED five-step MODEL — the ECONOMIC outcome for MOST construction CONTRACTS remains BROADLY similar (revenue RECOGNISED progressively as WORK is performed), but IT is now ANALYSED through the GENERAL over-time RECOGNITION criteria (Section 4) RATHER than a SEPARATE, dedicated STANDARD.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Variable Consideration and the Transaction Price</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Estimating uncertain elements of the price</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE the TRANSACTION price INCLUDES a VARIABLE element (DISCOUNTS, rebates, PENALTIES, or PERFORMANCE bonuses), the ENTERPRISE estimates the EXPECTED amount USING either the EXPECTED VALUE method or the MOST LIKELY amount METHOD, INCLUDING the ESTIMATE in the TRANSACTION price ONLY to the EXTENT it is HIGHLY probable a SIGNIFICANT reversal WILL NOT occur ONCE the UNCERTAINTY is RESOLVED.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Allocating the Transaction Price</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Based on relative standalone selling price</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE a CONTRACT contains MULTIPLE performance OBLIGATIONS, the TRANSACTION price is ALLOCATED to EACH obligation BASED on its RELATIVE STANDALONE selling PRICE — the PRICE at WHICH the enterprise WOULD sell that GOOD or SERVICE separately.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Allocating a Bundled Transaction Price</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Splitting a hardware-and-service bundle</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Equipment sold with a maintenance package</div><div class="wk-body">A company sells a bundle of equipment (standalone selling price RMB 900,000) and a 1-year maintenance service (standalone selling price RMB 100,000) for a combined RMB 950,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">The RMB 950,000 transaction PRICE is ALLOCATED based on RELATIVE standalone SELLING price: equipment = RMB 950,000 × (RMB 900,000 ÷ RMB 1,000,000) = <strong>RMB 855,000</strong> (recognised at the POINT the equipment is DELIVERED); maintenance = RMB 950,000 × (RMB 100,000 ÷ RMB 1,000,000) = <strong>RMB 95,000</strong> (recognised OVER the 1-year SERVICE period).</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Over-Time Recognition for a Construction Contract</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">The successor to the old percentage-of-completion method</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A bespoke industrial facility</div><div class="wk-body">A construction company builds a CUSTOM facility with NO alternative use, and an ENFORCEABLE right to payment for work completed to date, under a RMB 500,000,000 contract. By year end, 60% of the work is complete.</div><div class="wk-answer">Since the criteria for OVER-TIME recognition are MET, the company recognises revenue of RMB 500,000,000 × 60% = <strong>RMB 300,000,000</strong> for the year — the SAME general economic OUTCOME the OLD percentage-of-completion method under ASBE No. 15 would have PRODUCED, now analysed WITHIN this Standard's GENERAL five-step framework.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 14 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Disaggregation of revenue by category</span><span>Information about performance obligations, including timing of satisfaction</span><span>Significant judgements applied in determining the transaction price and its allocation</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Identifying distinct performance obligations within a bundled contract</span><span>Whether a performance obligation is satisfied over time or at a point in time</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Standalone selling prices used for allocation</span><span>Variable consideration estimates</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 15</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 14 vs IFRS 15</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 14 (2017 revision)</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 15</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Five-step model</span><span>YES</span><span>YES — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Construction contracts</span><span>Absorbed into the general model</span><span>Same — IAS 11 absorbed into IFRS 15</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED revision — CHINA'S adoption CLOSELY tracked IFRS 15's OWN international TIMELINE, a CONTRAST to slower-CONVERGING topics ELSEWHERE in the ASBE suite.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every revenue recognition event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Revenue recognition (over time or point in time)</span><span><span class="badge bp">IS</span> <span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>Based on satisfaction of performance obligations</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 15</span><span>Construction Contracts — the superseded, historical standard whose substance this revision absorbed</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Performance obligation</div><div class="glossary-def">A distinct promise within a contract to transfer a good or service to a customer, the unit of account for revenue recognition.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Standalone selling price</div><div class="glossary-def">The price at which a good or service would be sold separately, used to allocate a bundled transaction price.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe14 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
